  "result": "All 9 tests pass (6 existing plus the 3 new ones).\n\n**What I changed** in `wire/codec.py`:\n\n- **Added `encode_stream(records, fp)`.** It writes the header, then packs and writes each record individually while accumulating the CRC32 incrementally, then writes the footer. The output is byte-for-byte identical to `encode`, which I verified directly.\n- **Added `decode_stream(fp)`.** It reads the file object to the end and delegates to `decode`, so both APIs accept exactly the same format. Passing a text-mode file raises `CodecError`.\n- **Added `record_count(data)`.** It reads the count from the header and validates magic, version, total length, and checksum, but never unpacks records or builds dicts. Truncated or garbage input raises `CodecError` just as `decode` does.\n- **Refactored frame validation** into a shared `_check_frame` helper used by both `decode` and `record_count`, so the two cannot drift apart. Behavior of `encode` and `decode` is unchanged.\n\nNo files under `tests/` were modified. Note that `wire/codec.py` and `tests/test_t2.py` are both still untracked in git, so they will need to be added when you commit.",
